<section xml:id="grading">
  <title>Summary of Course Components</title>

  <introduction>
    <table xml:id="table-components">
      <title>Course components and the points each one is worth</title>
      <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor">
        <col width="28%"/>
        <col width="26%"/>
        <col width="46%"/>
        <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
          <cell>Course component</cell>
          <cell>Maximum points</cell>
          <cell>Date</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>Exam #1</cell>
          <cell>20</cell>
          <cell>Friday, October 9 (week 3)</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>Exam #2</cell>
          <cell>20</cell>
          <cell>Friday, October 30 (week 6)</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>Exam #3</cell>
          <cell>20</cell>
          <cell>Friday, November 20 (week 9)</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>Final Exam</cell>
          <cell>30</cell>
          <cell>December 7 <ndash/> 11, scheduled by the Registrar</cell>
        </row>
        <row bottom="minor">
          <cell>Assignments</cell>
          <cell>10</cell>
          <cell>See <xref ref="assignments" text="title"/></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>Total</cell>
          <cell>100</cell>
          <cell></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>
    </table>

    <p>
      The final examination period is December 7 <ndash/> 11. The Registrar's
      Office schedules the final exam; the date and time for each section, as
      set by the Registrar, are copied in <xref ref="table-final-exam"/>.
    </p>

    <p>
      <alert>Calculators of any kind are not permitted on the exams.</alert>
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="exam-topics">
    <title>Tentative List of Topics for the Exams</title>

    <p>
      The lists below are <alert>tentative</alert>. They show the topics I
      expect each midterm exam to cover, and I will confirm the exact coverage
      in class before each exam. Every topic links to its section in the
      skeletal notes, and each list matches the review problem set for that
      exam: the leftover problems on those topics, collected for review.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Exam #1</em> (Friday, October 9) <mdash/> see
      <url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-exercises-review1-practice.html">Review Problems #1</url>:
    </p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-parametrization.html">Parametrization of Curves</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-arc-length.html">Arc Length of a Curve</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-line-integrals.html">Line Integrals</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-vector-fields.html">Vector Fields and Line Integrals</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-conservative-fields.html">Path Independence, Conservative Fields, and Potential Functions</url></p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Exam #2</em> (Friday, October 30) <mdash/> see
      <url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-exercises-review2-practice.html">Review Problems #2</url>:
    </p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-double-integrals-rectangles.html">Double and Iterated Integrals Over Rectangles</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-double-integrals-general-regions.html">Double Integrals Over General Regions and Area by Double Integration</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-polar-coordinates.html">Polar Coordinates and Graphing Polar Equations</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-double-integrals-polar-form.html">Double Integrals in Polar Form</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-triple-integrals-rectangular.html">Triple Integrals in Rectangular Coordinates</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-triple-integrals-cylindrical.html">Triple Integrals in Cylindrical Coordinates</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-triple-integrals-spherical.html">Triple Integrals in Spherical Coordinates</url></p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Exam #3</em> (Friday, November 20) <mdash/> see
      <url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/sec-exercises-review3-practice.html">Review Problems #3</url>:
    </p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-mass-center-of-mass.html">Applications: Mass and Center of Mass</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/MATH14-Skeletal/section-jacobian-substitution.html">Substitution in Multiple Integrals and the Jacobian Determinant</url></p>
